---
description: Backend/FastAPI architecture rules
globs: backend/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Structure per module (app/modules/<name>/): models.py, schemas.py,
repository.py, service.py, router.py. Route handlers call service functions,
service functions call repository functions. Never put query logic in
service.py or business logic in repository.py.

Never expose SQLAlchemy models directly through API responses — always go
through a Pydantic schema in schemas.py.

Multi-tenancy: every organization-owned table has an organization_id column.
Every query touching such a table must filter by organization_id — never
trust organization_id from arbitrary request input; derive it from the
authenticated session/token context.

Module boundaries: a module may only import from app/core/ and its own
files. Never import another module's models.py, service.py, or repository.py
directly. backend/tool/verify_architecture.py enforces this — run it.

Error handling: raise the domain exceptions defined in app/core/exceptions.py
(NotFoundError, ValidationError, ConflictError, etc.) from service.py. Route
handlers (or a shared exception handler) map these to HTTP responses with
the stable JSON error shape: {"code": "...", "message": "...", "details": {}}.
Never let a raw exception or stack trace reach the client.

Never store secrets, tokens, or passwords in logs. Never put tokens or
passwords in URLs or query params.

Async SQLAlchemy only — no synchronous session usage in route handlers.

Do not scaffold new modules (jobs, screening, evidence, etc.) unless
explicitly asked. Do not add functionality beyond what the current task
specifies.
